   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging public and private sector investments in sustainable food (poultry) value chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project pioneers a blended finance strategy that strategically combines catalytic grant funding with private sector capital mobilized through local financial service providers (FSPs). This approach is designed not only to provide direct financing but to fundamentally transform the lending landscape for the poultry sector. The central objective is to achieve a financial leverage ratio of at least 1:8, meaning that every dollar of initial program funding will mobilize eight additional dollars of financing into the value chain. This leverage ratio demonstrates operational efficiency and unlocks capital at a scale sufficient to drive meaningful sectoral transformation. The financial solution is built around synergistic instruments, co-developed and rigorously refined in collaboration with partner FSPs and key stakeholders, based on actual market conditions.  UNCDF and IFAD will: # Develop and rollout of financial products earmarked for the poultry value chain actors # Train of farmers on business and financial literacy # Advocate for policies that facilitate the scaling up agricultural finance in Ethiopia  FAO will: # Conduct training on poultry husbandry for growers # Implement consumer education campaigns on the nutritional benefits of poultry products. # Support the implementation of biosecurity measures  UN</narrative>
  </description>
